WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.768
-Chelsea Handler. Come on, you
can't beat an audience, right?

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:05.605
-No, no, you cannot beat
an audience, Jimmy.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.940
-Thank you for being here
in person.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.775
I appreciate it.
-Well, I missed you.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.677
Desperately. No, no,
I don't miss you actively

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:13.245
'cause we're here together now.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.814
-But I missed you during COVID,
but I got to see you

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.116
a lot during COVID.
-You were very nice to me.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.219
You Zoomed in a few times
from your home.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.187
And I appreciate that.
-I was skiing.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.722
I was skiing in Whistler
when I was doing your show.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.458
So I would come in
from the ski mountain.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.460
You know, take my pants down
for the Zoom

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.295
and then just have my ski top
on the top.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.463
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.831
-I didn't know that.
I didn't know that. Yeah.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.735
-I like to do all my Zooms
pants-less just to get

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.604
men back for what they've done.
You know what I mean?

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.806
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.874
-I heard that you're on
a new health kick.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.776
Explain this to me.
-Well, it's not a health kick.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.978
I'm doing a 30-day detox
from alcohol

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:49.148
because someone called in
from my podcast.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:52.051
And she said she was having
trouble kind of detoxing

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.120
and I said I would do it
in solidarity with her.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.722
-Oh.
-But I did a 30-day cannabis

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.959
detox also, so now it's 30 days
of cannabis detox

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:03.463
and a 30-day alcohol detox,
two separate months.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.765
So I've lost two months of
my life due to this podcast.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:08.767
[ Laughter ]
And I'm over it. I'm over it.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.636
I can't wait to have --
And my friend's like, "If you do

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.039
30 days, you're gonna feel so
good, you're gonna go a year."

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.373
I'm like, "No, I won't."

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:15.775
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.744
But I love that you do that
to your fans.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.679
I mean, I love the podcast.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.381
"Dear Chelsea" is the podcast,
and it's fantastic.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.050
If you love podcasts
and you love Chelsea --

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.219
-I give out advice to people who
actually want advice from me.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.321
I mean, I've been giving out
unsolicited advice

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:31.223
a lot for a long time.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.159
-So this is solicited.
-This is when people actually

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.961
call in and they have
real-life problems

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.396
or really silly problems,
but either way, you know,

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:40.199
I like to encourage people
to be a little bit braver,

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.268
a little bit stronger,
like a big sister who's like,

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.170
"Go out and do that.
Leave that job.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.471
Leave that relationship.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.407
Do whatever you need to
make yourself

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.509
like a little bit more
successful and confident."

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.910
-Yeah, I love that.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.645
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.480
-That's one of the reasons
why we love you.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.315
But I think you're
just brutally honest.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.718
You're always honest.
and that's the best thing

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.354
you can do because then --
clearly, you didn't even lie

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.688
when we played the game
where you can lie.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.924
-No, I mean -- and you know how
I feel about games.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.225
-No, we didn't have to
get into it.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.594
-No, I'll get into it.
I can't stand playing games.

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:10.163
-I know you don't like them.
I know. But I like to watch you.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.799
-But you force me.
-I don't force you.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.767
You could say no.
-Oh, can I?

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.503
Can I say no?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.137
-We probably wouldn't book you
on the show if you said no.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.671
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.671 --> 00:02:21.141
Of course, you can do whatever
you want on the show,

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.742
but I love watching
you play a game

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.843
'cause you don't like
playing the game.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.010
That makes it more fun to watch.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.779
-Yeah, it's fun to watch you
watching me

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.915
struggle playing a game.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:33.285
-Hey, I follow you on the
Instagram and all that stuff,

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:34.921
and you posted something.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.856
I go, "That was so beautiful."

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.457
You said, "I'm finally in love."

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:40.192
-I am! I'm in love!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:41.460
-Buddy.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.162
Hey!

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.498
-How cute is that?
-Couldn't be cuter.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:48.634
And, you know, every time you
come on we talk about something,

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.569
about dating or relationships.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:52.538
You're in love.
-I know, and I have to say,

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:55.108
if I fell in love at
the age of 46, you guys,

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.209
I have hope for every person
in this world.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.812
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes, yes.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:03.249
It's never -- It's never too --
I was really just kind of like,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.652
men were very discouraging
these past couple of years,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.520
especially, you know,
straight white men.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.557
And I was like, "Oh, God, who
I am going to end up with?"

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.824
You know?

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.093
And then I had my friend Jo Koy,

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.861
who was in my life
for a very long time.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.530
He used to be on my old show,
"Chelsea Lately."

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.166
-Yeah.
-And he and I were friends.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:23.769
And then he kept showing up
and showing up and showing up.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.271
And I was like, "Mmm-mm-mmm."

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.240
[ Laughter ]
And then one day, I just looked

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.541
at him and I thought,
"Oh, that's my guy."

00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:30.943
[ Audience aws ]
Yeah.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:34.246
So he's like my best buddy
and then I also, you know,

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:37.483
get to have sex with him.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:41.220
Fun times. So, anyone, if you
have a friend in your life

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.656
that you think you're not into
or not attracted to,

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.025
just remember my story
and to be open-minded,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.394
because little things can tap
you on the shoulder

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.728
and then all of a sudden,
you see something

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:51.664
through a different lens,
and I mean,

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.800
I would never talk about a man
like this unless I meant it.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.402
-I love it, buddy.
I'm so happy for you.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.071
[ Applause ]

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.340
And he's a brilliant comedian
too, so that must be so fun.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.975
-And I'm pregnant.

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.878
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.981
I'm not pregnant.
I'm not pregnant.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.081
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-See?

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.282
You know how the play the game.

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:12.952
I want to talk about
your stand-up tour,

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.921
"Vaccinated and Horny Tour."

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.990
The name got a laugh
every time I said it.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.791
You always think of good titles.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.992
You're at the Beacon Theatre.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.627
-I'm playing two shows at
the Beacon this weekend.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:24.129
I'm doing Albany, Boston -- I'm
going all over to the country.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.831
And I'm announcing
more dates soon,

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.167
and it's been so fun
to be on the road.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.803
-What's it like?
-Well, it's just like this.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.205
I mean, there is nothing
that replaces a live audience.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.108
So it's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.143
Yeah.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.679
-We need it. We need it.
Thank you for doing this.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.047
-Well, you're welcome, Jimmy.
The whole world is welcome.

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:43.816
[ Laughter ]
-I really mean it.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.017
Honestly, we needed to laugh.
We need something to laugh at.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:47.653
-Yeah. We do, and it's so nice
to be a reason

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:49.688
that people -- you know,
to bring people back together,

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.258
many for the first time
in like a year or two.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.427
And so I named the tour
"Vaccinated and Horny" 'cause

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.061
that's how a lot of
single people were feeling,

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:57.562
and married people,
quite frankly,

00:04:57.562 --> 00:05:00.800
after the thick of COVID.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.902
Hopefully we're through
the thick of it.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.737
And then, so I'm still
vaccinated and I'm still horny,

00:05:05.737 --> 00:05:07.740
just now for one person
instead of the world.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.208
-There you go, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:14.013
You're doing a very cool thing
that I thought was interesting

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.816
for flight attendants.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.117
Flight attendants, you guys.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.219
We have to respect
our flight attendants. I was --

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.288
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Absolutely we have to.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.789
What is going on?

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:26.959
-Oh, I don't know, but I got on
my first flight in a long time

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.395
a couple months ago,
and the announcement

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:32.297
that the captain had to make
over the loudspeaker

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:34.466
was so embarrassing to society.

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:37.436
He's like, "Okay, everyone,
please make sure your masks

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.972
are over your nose, and when you
take a bite of food,

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.073
you can lower your mask.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:42.241
And then when you're done
chewing,

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.143
put your mask again
over your nose.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.146
Please do not hit or touch
the flight attendants."

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:50.616
And I was just devastated
for them because I just thought,

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.685
"What have we come to
that we can't" --

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.720
And these poor people that
become flight attendants,

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.023
they're just, you know,
trying to have a nice job

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.557
where they can travel
to fun places.

00:05:58.557 --> 00:05:59.692
Now they have to take jiu-jitsu

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:00.960
and duct-tape people
to their seats?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.861
[ Laughter ]
-It's insane.

00:06:02.861 --> 00:06:06.098
-I mean, what kind of idiot,
moron gets on a plane

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:09.201
and is like, "I won't do it.
I won't wear a mask."

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:11.070
You know, as they're taping you
to your seat,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.438
what are you thinking?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.873
You're like, "Oh, my God,
I can't wait

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.608
till my granddaughter
sees this video."

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:18.410
-I mean, exactly right.
But here's what you do.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.279
You step in and you go, "Hey,
if you're a flight attendant,

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.015
DM me and I'll give you
free tickets to my show."

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:26.919
-Yeah, yeah. So we have
a lot of flight attendants

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.487
coming to all my shows.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.423
The Beacon especially
this weekend, I think we have

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.025
100 flying in from all different
places all over the world.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.927
So yeah, we helped --
If you're a flight attendant

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:37.730
and you didn't get a ticket,
it's because we were bombarded.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.232
I'm announcing new dates soon

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.999
and we'll try and get you
in the second round.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:43.335
But we are --
Yeah, flight attendants,

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:44.904
we've got to give our love
to them.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.405
Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.007
-I got to tell you,
every time you come on,

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.641
you're the most fun person.

00:06:49.641 --> 00:06:51.577
We love you.
Chelsea Handler, everybody.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:54.513
Get tickets for
"Vaccinated and Horny Tour"

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.582
at chelseahandler.com.

